.TH EITAAS-GUI 1 "August 2026" "EITaaS-Linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eitaas-gui \- EITaaS Connect, a graphical readiness, profile import, and connect helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eitaas-gui
.RI [ FILE.rdpw ]
.br
.B eitaas-gui --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eitaas-gui
(EITaaS Connect, application id org.eitaas.Helper) is a GTK 4/Libadwaita
window over the same application API as
.BR eitaas (1).
It is installed by the optional eitaas-linux-gui package and has three pages.
.PP
.B Readiness
shows the
.B eitaas doctor
result as plain-language rows: bundled remote desktop client, desktop session,
smart-card service, smart-card reader, card middleware, and diagnostic
tools. Each row states Ready, Needs attention, Not ready, or Not
checked, explains what was checked, and names the package or command that
fixes it. Commands are shown with a copy button; nothing privileged is run.
.PP
.B Profile
lists the steps for exporting a .rdpw profile from the web client, opens a
file chooser to import one, and lists the imported profiles with a selector
for the one Connect uses and a Remove action. Import moves the file into the
private store, restricts it to the user, and makes it the default; see
PROFILE STORE in
.BR eitaas (1).
.PP
.B Connect
starts
.B eitaas-remmina
with the selected profile. The button is disabled only on hard failures: the
launcher or its private client binary missing, or no imported profile.
Warnings never disable it. While the client runs the page
shows the phase and a Cancel button; sign-in and the PIN prompt happen in the
client window. Closing the window while the client runs asks whether to
disconnect and quit or keep working. When the client exits with a non-zero
status the page shows the last
.B smartcard-auth:
reason-code and Remmina warning lines from the redacted session log, the
log's path, and a "Copy diagnostic log" button that places the whole
redacted log on the clipboard; see SESSION LOGS in
.BR eitaas (1).
.PP
The first run opens on the Readiness page. After a run whose checks all
passed (warnings allowed), and while a default profile exists, later starts
open directly on the Connect page; the checks still run on every start, in
the background. If a check that passed before now fails, a dialog names it
and, when dismissed, switches to the Readiness page. The recorded pass is a
timestamp and summary hash only; see FILES.
.PP
When
.I FILE.rdpw
is given, or the desktop entry opens a file of MIME type
application/x-eitaas-rdpw, the Profile page shows a banner offering to import
that file. Nothing is imported or connected until Import and then Connect are
pressed.
.PP
.B --version
prints the version and exits without a display.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/eitaas-remmina/profiles/
Imported profiles (directory mode 0700, files mode 0600).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/eitaas/profiles.ini
The default profile name, as
.B [profiles] default = NAME
(mode 0600).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/eitaas-remmina/logs/
Redacted per-connection session logs (directory mode 0700, files mode 0600,
newest five kept).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/eitaas-gui/last-readiness-pass.json
The last readiness pass (directory mode 0700, file mode 0600): an ISO-8601
timestamp and a SHA-256 hash of the readiness summary, nothing else. It only
selects the startup page; deleting it is harmless.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Re-check readiness.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Choose a .rdpw file to import.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Return
Connect.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eitaas (1),
.B eitaas-remmina
